DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
       NNoottee: This system call is present only before Linux 2.6.

       If  _t_a_b_l_e  is  NULL,  ggeett__kkeerrnneell__ssyymmss()  returns  the number of symbols
       available for query.  Otherwise, it fills in a table of structures:

           struct kernel_sym {
               unsigned long value;
               char          name[60];
           };

       The symbols are interspersed with magic symbols of  the  form  ##_m_o_d_u_l_e_‐
       _n_a_m_e with the kernel having an empty name.  The value associated with a
       symbol of this form is the address at which the module is loaded.

       The symbols exported from each module follow their magic module tag and
       the modules are returned in the reverse of the order in which they were
       loaded.

